  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What Do I Do & When Do I Act Again?",
      "items": [
        "1. Open the issue, post /epure plan, and reply in plain text to Grill rounds until settled",
        "2. Run /epure to-spec (reply in plain text to adjust the spec if needed), then /epure to-tickets",
        "3. Run /epure approve to sign the mandate, then wait until the final feature/* -> dev PR is ready to Squash & Merge"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What Happens Automatically Behind the Scenes?",
      "items": [
        "Commits GLOSSARY.md, ADRs & Spec on plan/* with zero-context Goldfish audit, then wires native GitHub sub_issues & blocked_by",
        "Directly merges plan/* -> feature/* on approve, locks spec_sha, and executes each ticket in the 2-phase kernel sandbox",
        "Suspends at zero runner cost during external CI (waiting_ticket_ci), runs Stage 3 dev review + AI squash, and runs EpicConvergenceAudit (Phase 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "How Do Autofix Loops, Conflicts & Steering Work?",
      "items": [
        "Automatic Autofix (1..3 tries): if Stage 1 tests, external CI, or reviewers fail, EPURE patches and re-verifies automatically",
        "Git Conflict Sync: comment /epure sync (or /epure rebase) to merge dev -> feature/* -> task/* with 3-way resolution",
        "Escalation & Control: if paused in needs-human, push a fix or clarify and run /epure continue (plus /epure status or /epure cancel anytime)"
      ]
    }
  ]
